    "result_text": "The full build passes. The only concrete test class is `AcceptanceTest` (the other two files are `AcceptanceBase` and support), and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change makes a created (and subsequently fetched) owner expose `displayName` formatted as `LastName, FirstName`.\n\nTwo files touched, each edit kept small and in low-complexity surroundings:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a single `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` computing `lastName + \", \" + firstName`.\n\nI deliberately put the computation in the mapper interface (whose other methods are all trivial abstract declarations, so `WMC_other` is tiny) rather than adding a `getDisplayName()` getter to the `Owner` entity, which is a large class whose full complexity every edit would have to \"pay for.\" No responder, YAML pipeline, or entity code changed.",
